---
title: Navigation flow — one keypress, end to end
---
%% Verified against the tree on 2026-09-13.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant KB as Platform capture<br/>keyboard.js · DispatchKeyEvent · PressesBegan
    participant BIS as BlazorInputService
    participant SM as ShortcutManager
    participant RM as WebHostShortcutRemap
    participant CD as CommandDispatcher
    participant MS as ModalStack
    participant NE as NavigationEngine
    participant VM as ViewportManager
    participant ST as WorkspaceStore
    participant EB as EventBus
    participant AFC as AccessibilityFeedbackCoordinator
    participant SFR as SpeechFeedbackRouter
    participant SMM as SonificationManager
    participant TD as ITactileDriver

    Note over RM,SM: WebHost only, once at startup
    RM->>SM: a saved pre-2026-09-05 Ctrl+Shift+letter chord becomes Alt+Shift+letter,<br/>and browser-reserved Ctrl+T, Ctrl+W, Ctrl+Tab are removed
    Note right of RM: in memory only — shortcuts.json stays portable<br/>and F1 reads the live profile, so Help is never wrong.<br/>The default profile is already Alt+Shift, so a fresh install is untouched.

    U->>KB: press a key
    KB->>BIS: key + modifiers
    BIS->>SM: resolve
    SM-->>BIS: SystemCommand (or None — the key passes through)
    BIS->>CD: dispatch

    alt movement along the X axis (Left/Right, Home/End, Ctrl+Left/Right)
        CD->>NE: navigate
        NE->>ST: NavigateAction
        NE->>EB: FeedbackRequestEvent
    else viewport ([ ] - = Shift+[ Shift+])
        CD->>VM: pan / zoom / change the pan step
        VM->>ST: viewport change
    else series and component (Up/Down, PageUp/Down, Ctrl+Up/Down)
        CD->>ST: focus change
    else pane — the next Y axis (Alt+PageUp / Alt+PageDown, never Ctrl+PageUp: browsers own it)
        CD->>ST: focus the first series of the neighbouring pane, then name the pane
    else a panel or modal (Alt+letter, F-keys)
        CD->>EB: Open...Event
    else Escape with a dialog open
        CD->>MS: which dialog is on top?
        MS-->>CD: the top entry — the only one Escape may close
        CD->>EB: CloseModal for that dialog, and focus returns to the one beneath, or to the chart
    else drawing (Alt+Shift+letter — sequential anchoring)
        CD->>EB: AddDrawingEvent — one press per anchor, no Enter to confirm
    end

    par speech
        ST-->>AFC: StateStream
        EB-->>AFC: FeedbackRequestEvent
        AFC->>SFR: format for the focused thing
        SFR-->>U: speak (interrupting or queued, per channel)
    and audio
        ST-->>SMM: StateStream
        SMM->>SMM: NavigationSonifier.SyncNavigationSlots
        SMM-->>U: voice slots 0-15 — pitch, timbre, stereo position
    and tactile
        VM-->>TD: slice the device-sized window
        TD-->>U: pins
    end

    Note over AFC,SMM: One path per modality. Nothing else writes navigation<br/>voice slots, and nothing else decides what a move says.
